4. Chatbot Features (v0.1)

Security & Compliance

Access Control & Eligibility: Data access is restricted based on the user's profile. For example, a standard user is limited to viewing their own rights, while a manager can access their team's data.

Data Privacy: Sensitive data filtering through mechanisms designed to prevent the exposure of confidential information. Guarantee that the Chatbot processes data strictly within the secure MyIAM infrastructure, with no data transfer to LLM models external to the organization.

Audit Trail: Secure archiving of all interactions to allow for comprehensive auditing and traceability.

Intelligent Response Engine (NLU & RAG)

Natural Language Understanding (NLU): The ability to interpret user intent regardless of the jargon used, ensuring fluid and intuitive interaction.

RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) on IAM Knowledge Base: Intelligent information extraction from official documentation (procedures, guides, FAQs) to provide precise, sourced, and consistently up-to-date answers.

Connectivity & Tracking (MyIAM Data Read)

Real-time Status Query (TBC): Secure connection to MyIAM to retrieve and display the progress of a specific request via its Request ID.

Bottleneck Identification: Ability to identify the current approver or the team in charge of the ticket to provide the user with clear direction.

User Journey Assistance (Guidance & Workflow)

Step-by-step Guidance Generator: Interactive guidance to direct the user to the correct MyIAM form or tab based on their specific needs.

Smart Redirection to Support: In cases where self-service resolution fails, the chatbot provides direct links to ServiceNow tickets or contacts for IAM Operations.

User Experience & Continuous Improvement

Contextualization: Ability to maintain conversation context (short-term memory of previous exchanges) so the user does not have to repeat information already provided.

Interaction Logging & Feedback Loop: Anonymized data collection on interactions and user feedback ("Helpful/Not helpful" buttons) to identify documentary gaps and enrich the knowledge base.

Communication (Recertification)

Recertification Campaign Support: Distribution of information regarding campaign deadlines, compliance reminders, and best practices to support the concerned users.









