7. Risks & Mitigations

Risk 1: Low Adoption Rate Users continue to send emails to support instead of using the Chatbot.

Mitigation: Targeted communication campaigns, and direct integration of the Chatbot into the MyIAM Portal for maximum accessibility and visibility.

Risk 2: Data Breach or Unauthorized Access Accidental leakage of sensitive data or unauthorized access to management-level information.

Mitigation: Implementation of robust Access Control and profile-based filtering to ensure users only see data they are eligible to view.

Risk 3: AI Hallucinations The Chatbot could generate incorrect answers or "invent" procedures, misleading the user.

Mitigation: Use of RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) architecture, ensuring the model only answers based on provided official documentation. Integration of a Feedback Button for users to report inaccuracies.

Risk 4: Knowledge Gaps / Unresolved Queries The Chatbot may not find an answer if the question is too specific or if the information is missing from the FAQ/MyIAM database.

Mitigation: In cases of low confidence scores or a total lack of information, the Chatbot must not "hallucinate" a response. Instead, it will automatically redirect the user to the support team (via ServiceNow or the IAM Mailbox).







